{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"code":"bipartition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"First fit in index order (the lexicographically first proper colouring of all) when it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"already optimal. Otherwise each vertex in turn takes the least colour its prefix still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"extends with (k-colouring’s self-reduction to its decision problem): a Kempe swap of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last colouring found when one avoids the prefix, else DSatur branch and bound over the parts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the prefix that the vertex touches (on sparse components with conflict-directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backjumping and restarts). Khuller and Vazirani show the lexicographically first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four-colouring of a planar graph is NP-hard to find, though some four-colouring is found in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polynomial time. It can be far slower than ","type":"text"},{"code":"minimumColoring()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and its time grows steeply","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with n even on sparse 3-colourable graphs. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"ColoringModule","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactColoring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ColoringModule\/ExactColoring.swift#L622"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P14ColoringModuleE029lexicographicallyFirstMinimumC0AD0C0VyxGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}]},"references":{"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14ColoringModule0A0V","text":"Coloring"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumcoloring()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum colouring of the simple graph: on each connected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, of all its colourings with its own chromatic number of colours, the one whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colour vector (in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order) is lexicographically least, Khuller and Vazirani’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically first k-colouring (1991) with k = the component’s χ. So within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component colours appear in order of first use, colour classes are numbered by their least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, a bipartite component is coloured by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition()"},{"type":"text","text":" sides (left 0), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"colorCount == chromaticNumber()"},{"type":"text","text":". Components are not coupled: a bipartite one keeps two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"colours beside a triangle."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()","type":"topic"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"collection","title":"ColoringModule"},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"type":"topic","title":"Graph","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[]},"doc://ColoringModule/documentation/ColoringModule/Coloring":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Coloring","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Coloring","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloring","abstract":[{"text":"A proper colouring of a graph’s vertices by the colours ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<colorCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each of which is used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(unless preset colours skip some): the result of ","type":"text"},{"code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:presetColor:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(order:)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumColoring()"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumColoring()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"Coloring","identifier":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/Coloring","type":"topic"}}}